{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Independent non-author exact-SHA documentation review: FAIL.\n\nReviewed final commit 602f02feb267df7d087392b2405190e7855e432b against exact parent 7724d24732672114bbc0394a1d19476fa8932b7e. All six parent blobs are byte-identical to the ticket's pinned 0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e basis. The changed-path set is exactly the six declared paths.\n\nStage 1 — Spec compliance: FAIL. Normalized executable ASTs, non-docstring runtime strings, assertions, directive order, and shebang state are unchanged, and 96 focused tests passed. However, the patch changes 50 prose blocks while the ticket declares 49. tests/scripts/bridge/test_jira_capability_probe.py:L1-L5 is an unmatched, unscoped module-docstring hunk; the ticket's scope for that file begins at L18. This blocks approval under the listed-block and unmatched-hunk closure rules.\n\nStage 2 — Documentation quality: FAIL against the strict per-row shrink criterion. Seven declared rows are not shorter under the receipt's natural-word count: ACLI L520 (2 -> 8), L591 (2 -> 6), L639 (4 -> 5); alert-display L59-L61 (1 -> 2), L226 (12 -> 12); capability-probe L26-L28 (1 -> 2), L168-L170 (1 -> 2). Their replacement prose is semantically sound, but the ticket requires every row to shrink. All other rows remove repetition, history, ornament, or obvious narration while preserving their contracts.\n\nStage 3 — Domain integrity: PASS / not applicable. No executable AST, type, identifier, state representation, or domain boundary changed.\n\nIndependent validation: 96 focused tests passed in 132.82 seconds. Path-scoped Ruff, Ruff format, comment hygiene, git diff integrity, normalized AST, and exact directive checks passed. Full local make verify was intentionally omitted under the documentation-only session direction; Gerrit CI remains the repository-wide gate.\n\nThe TSV contains one row for each of the 50 actual edited prose blocks. A zero-word final row cites the preserved adjacent-code anchor at the deletion point. Totals are 2170 -> 696 words, but aggregate shrink cannot satisfy a failing per-row criterion.\n\nstable_block_id\tbefore_citation\tfinal_citation\tpreserved_contract_or_consumer\tdirectives_exact\tbefore_words\tafter_words\tsemantic-preservation\tbloat-removal\tscope-compliance\treviewer_session\ntests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py#S:L1-L22\t7724d24732672114bbc0394a1d19476fa8932b7e:tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py:L1-L22\t602f02feb267df7d087392b2405190e7855e432b:tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py:L1-L5\tPytest preserves ACLI field forwarding, command and payload shape, REST routing, and sanitizer contracts for this block.\tPASS\t133\t42\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\t/root/implement_core_test_comments\ntests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py#S:L34-L49\t7724d24732672114bbc0394a1d19476fa8932b7e:tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py:L34-L49\t602f02feb267df7d087392b2405190e7855e432b:tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py:L18-L25\tPytest preserves ACLI field forwarding, command and payload shape, REST routing, and sanitizer contracts for this block.\tPASS\t81\t24\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\t/root/implement_core_test_comments\ntests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py#S:L181-L196\t7724d24732672114bbc0394a1d19476fa8932b7e:tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py:L181-L196\t602f02feb267df7d087392b2405190e7855e432b:tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py:L158-L165\tPytest preserves ACLI field forwarding, command and payload shape, REST routing, and sanitizer contracts for this block.\tPASS\t104\t39\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\t/root/implement_core_test_comments\ntests/